---
title: "A9-b  States of one audit finding on a transaction"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  direction TB
  %% QUESTION THIS DIAGRAM ANSWERS: a transaction was questioned by the auditor. In which state is the finding now, and what are the possible next states?
  %% SOURCES: the notices, the settlement, the appeal levels, the Notice of Finality of Decision and the COA Order of Execution [COA2009-006] (Rules and Regulations on the Settlement of Accounts, COA Circular No. 2009-006).
  %% FROM THE AUDITING CODE OF 1978: a suspension that is not explained within ninety days becomes a disallowance [PD1445 s.82]. Appeal from the decision of an auditor within six months [PD1445 s.48]. The Commission decides within sixty days [PD1445 s.49]. Petition to the Supreme Court within thirty days [PD1445 s.50]. A decision that is not appealed is final and executory [PD1445 s.51]. A settled account may be opened again within three years [PD1445 s.52]. A disallowance is recorded in the books of the agency only when it is final and executory, as a receivable from the persons liable [GAM-V1 Ch.6 s.46].
  %% LIMIT: the Code names the Commission as the body of appeal. The rules of 2009 place a Director before the Commission Proper [COA2009-006]. The rules of procedure of COA set the present periods, and I did not open them.
  %% GENERAL KNOWLEDGE, NOT OPENED IN A SOURCE HERE: the Audit Observation Memorandum as the first step, and the referral to the Ombudsman.

  state "Transaction paid, in the accounts" as PAID
  state "Audit Observation Memorandum issued" as AOM
  state "Closed: explanation accepted" as OK1
  state "Notice of Suspension" as NS
  state "Notice of Disallowance or Notice of Charge" as ND
  state "Settled: requirement met or amount paid" as SET
  state "On appeal to the Cluster or Regional Director" as AP1
  state "On review by the Commission Proper" as AP2
  state "Before the Supreme Court" as SC
  state "Lifted: appeal granted" as LIFT
  state "Final: Notice of Finality of Decision" as NFD
  state "COA Order of Execution" as COE
  state "Referred for administrative or criminal action" as REF

  [*] --> PAID
  PAID --> AOM: auditor finds a deficiency
  PAID --> [*]: no finding
  AOM --> OK1: management explains
  AOM --> NS: a requirement is missing
  AOM --> ND: expense not allowed, or revenue not collected in full
  NS --> SET: requirement met in time
  NS --> ND: not explained within 90 days
  ND --> SET: persons liable pay
  ND --> AP1: persons liable appeal (within six months)
  AP1 --> LIFT: granted
  AP1 --> AP2: denied, petition for review
  AP2 --> LIFT: granted
  AP2 --> SC: denied, petition to the Supreme Court (within 30 days)
  AP2 --> NFD: denied, no further petition
  SC --> LIFT: court reverses
  SC --> NFD: court affirms
  ND --> NFD: no appeal in time
  NFD --> COE: amount still unpaid
  COE --> SET: paid, or withheld from pay
  NFD --> REF: facts show an offence
  OK1 --> [*]
  SET --> [*]
  LIFT --> [*]
  REF --> [*]
